#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:1
msgid "ThinLTO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:7
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:9
msgid ""
"*ThinLTO* compilation is a new type of LTO that is both scalable and "
"incremental. *LTO* (Link Time Optimization) achieves better runtime "
"performance through whole-program analysis and cross-module optimization. "
"However, monolithic LTO implements this by merging all input into a single "
"module, which is not scalable in time or memory, and also prevents fast "
"incremental compiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:16
msgid ""
"In ThinLTO mode, as with regular LTO, clang emits LLVM bitcode after the "
"compile phase. The ThinLTO bitcode is augmented with a compact summary of "
"the module. During the link step, only the summaries are read and merged "
"into a combined summary index, which includes an index of function locations "
"for later cross-module function importing. Fast and efficient whole-program "
"analysis is then performed on the combined summary index."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:23
msgid ""
"However, all transformations, including function importing, occur later when "
"the modules are optimized in fully parallel backends. By default, [linkers]"
"(#linkers) that support ThinLTO are set up to launch the ThinLTO backends in "
"threads. So the usage model is not affected as the distinction between the "
"fast serial thin link step and the backends is transparent to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:30
msgid ""
"For more information on the ThinLTO design and current performance, see the "
"LLVM blog post [ThinLTO: Scalable and Incremental LTO](http://blog.llvm."
"org/2016/06/thinlto-scalable-and-incremental-lto.html). While tuning is "
"still in progress, results in the blog post show that ThinLTO already "
"performs well compared to LTO, in many cases matching the performance "
"improvement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:36
msgid "Current Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:38
msgid "Clang/LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:42
msgid ""
"The 3.9 release of clang includes ThinLTO support. However, ThinLTO is under "
"active development, and new features, improvements and bugfixes are being "
"added for the next release. For the latest ThinLTO support, [build a recent "
"version of clang and LLVM](https://llvm.org/docs/CMake.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:47
msgid "Linkers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:53
msgid "ThinLTO is currently supported for the following linkers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:55
msgid ""
"**gold (via the gold-plugin)**: Similar to monolithic LTO, this requires "
"using a [gold linker configured with plugins enabled](https://llvm.org/docs/"
"GoldPlugin.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:58
msgid "**ld64**: Starting with [Xcode 8](https://developer.apple.com/xcode/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:60
msgid "**lld**: Starting with r284050 for ELF, r298942 for COFF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:63 ../../../ThinLTO.md:258
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:65
msgid "Basic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:67
msgid ""
"To utilize ThinLTO, simply add the -flto=thin option to compile and link. E."
"g."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:74
msgid ""
"When using lld-link, the -flto option need only be added to the compile step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:81
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier, by default the linkers will launch the ThinLTO backend "
"threads in parallel, passing the resulting native object files back to the "
"linker for the final native link. As such, the usage model is the same as "
"non-LTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:86
msgid "With gold, if you see an error during the link of the form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:92
msgid ""
"Then either gold was not configured with plugins enabled, or clang was not "
"built with `-DLLVM_BINUTILS_INCDIR` set properly. See the instructions for "
"the [LLVM gold plugin](https://llvm.org/docs/GoldPlugin.html#how-to-build-"
"it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:97
msgid "Controlling Backend Parallelism"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:101
msgid ""
"By default, the ThinLTO link step will launch as many threads in parallel as "
"there are cores. If the number of cores can't be computed for the "
"architecture, then it will launch `std::thread::hardware_concurrency` number "
"of threads in parallel. For machines with hyper-threading, this is the total "
"number of virtual cores. For some applications and machine configurations "
"this may be too aggressive, in which case the amount of parallelism can be "
"reduced to `N` via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:110
msgid "gold: `-Wl,-plugin-opt,jobs=N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:112
msgid "ld64: `-Wl,-mllvm,-threads=N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:114
msgid "ld.lld, ld64.lld: `-Wl,--thinlto-jobs=N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:116
msgid "lld-link: `/opt:lldltojobs=N`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:119
msgid "Other possible values for `N` are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:121
msgid "0: Use one thread per physical core (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:123
msgid "1: Use a single thread only (disable multi-threading)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:125
msgid "all: Use one thread per logical core (uses all hyper-threads)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:128
msgid "Incremental"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:132
msgid ""
"ThinLTO supports fast incremental builds through the use of a cache, which "
"currently must be enabled through a linker option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:135
msgid "gold (as of LLVM 4.0): `-Wl,-plugin-opt,cache-dir=/path/to/cache`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:137
msgid ""
"ld64 (supported since clang 3.9 and Xcode 8) and Mach-O ld64.lld (as of LLVM "
"15.0): `-Wl,-cache_path_lto,/path/to/cache`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:140
msgid "ELF ld.lld (as of LLVM 5.0): `-Wl,--thinlto-cache-dir=/path/to/cache`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:142
msgid "COFF lld-link (as of LLVM 6.0): `/lldltocache:/path/to/cache`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:145
msgid "Cache Pruning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:147
msgid ""
"To help keep the size of the cache under control, ThinLTO supports cache "
"pruning. Cache pruning is supported with gold, ld64, and lld, but currently "
"only gold and lld allow you to control the policy with a policy string. The "
"cache policy must be specified with a linker option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:152
msgid "gold (as of LLVM 6.0): `-Wl,-plugin-opt,cache-policy=POLICY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:154
msgid ""
"ELF ld.lld (as of LLVM 5.0), Mach-O ld64.lld (as of LLVM 15.0): `-Wl,--"
"thinlto-cache-policy=POLICY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:156
msgid "COFF lld-link (as of LLVM 6.0): `/lldltocachepolicy:POLICY`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:159
msgid ""
"A policy string is a series of key-value pairs separated by `:` characters. "
"Possible key-value pairs are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:162
msgid ""
"`cache_size=X%`: The maximum size for the cache directory is `X` percent of "
"the available space on the disk. Set to 100 to indicate no limit, 50 to "
"indicate that the cache size will not be left over half the available disk "
"space. A value over 100 is invalid. A value of 0 disables the percentage "
"size-based pruning. The default is 75%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:168
msgid ""
"`cache_size_bytes=X`, `cache_size_bytes=Xk`, `cache_size_bytes=Xm`, "
"`cache_size_bytes=Xg`: Sets the maximum size for the cache directory to `X` "
"bytes (or KB, MB, GB respectively). A value over the amount of available "
"space on the disk will be reduced to the amount of available space. A value "
"of 0 disables the byte size-based pruning. The default is no byte size-based "
"pruning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:175
msgid ""
"Note that ThinLTO will apply both size-based pruning policies "
"simultaneously, and changing one does not affect the other. For example, a "
"policy of `cache_size_bytes=1g` on its own will cause both the 1GB and "
"default 75% policies to be applied unless the default `cache_size` is "
"overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:180
msgid ""
"`cache_size_files=X`: Set the maximum number of files in the cache "
"directory. Set to 0 to indicate no limit. The default is 1000000 files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:184
msgid ""
"`prune_after=Xs`, `prune_after=Xm`, `prune_after=Xh`: Sets the expiration "
"time for cache files to `X` seconds (or minutes, hours respectively). When a "
"file hasn't been accessed for `prune_after` seconds, it is removed from the "
"cache. A value of 0 disables the expiration-based pruning. The default is 1 "
"week."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:190
msgid ""
"`prune_interval=Xs`, `prune_interval=Xm`, `prune_interval=Xh`: Sets the "
"pruning interval to `X` seconds (or minutes, hours respectively). This is "
"intended to be used to avoid scanning the directory too often. It does not "
"impact the decision of which files to prune. A value of 0 forces the scan to "
"occur. The default is every 20 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:196
msgid "Clang Bootstrap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:198
msgid ""
"To [bootstrap clang/LLVM](https://llvm.org/docs/AdvancedBuilds."
"html#bootstrap-builds) with ThinLTO, follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:201
msgid ""
"The host [compiler](#compiler) must be a version of clang that supports "
"ThinLTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:202
msgid ""
"The host [linker](#linker) must support ThinLTO (and in the case of gold, "
"must be [configured with plugins enabled](https://llvm.org/docs/GoldPlugin."
"html))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:204
msgid ""
"Use the following additional [CMake variables](https://llvm.org/docs/CMake."
"html#options-and-variables) when configuring the bootstrap compiler build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:207 ../../../ThinLTO.md:215
msgid "`-DLLVM_ENABLE_LTO=Thin`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:208
msgid "`-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/path/to/host/clang`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:209
msgid "`-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/path/to/host/clang++`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:210
msgid "`-DCMAKE_RANLIB=/path/to/host/llvm-ranlib`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:211
msgid "`-DCMAKE_AR=/path/to/host/llvm-ar`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:213
msgid "Or, on Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:216
msgid "`-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=/path/to/host/clang-cl.exe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:217
msgid "`-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=/path/to/host/clang-cl.exe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:218
msgid "`-DCMAKE_LINKER=/path/to/host/lld-link.exe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:219
msgid "`-DCMAKE_RANLIB=/path/to/host/llvm-ranlib.exe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:220
msgid "`-DCMAKE_AR=/path/to/host/llvm-ar.exe`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:222
msgid ""
"To use additional linker arguments for controlling the backend [parallelism]"
"(#parallelism) or enabling [incremental](#incremental) builds of the "
"bootstrap compiler, after configuring the build, modify the resulting "
"CMakeCache.txt file in the build directory. Specify any additional linker "
"options after `CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS:STRING=`. Note the configure may fail "
"if linker plugin options are instead specified directly in the previous step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:229
msgid ""
"The `BOOTSTRAP_LLVM_ENABLE_LTO=Thin` will enable ThinLTO for stage 2 and "
"stage 3 in case the compiler used for stage 1 does not support the ThinLTO "
"option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:233
msgid "Integrated Distributed ThinLTO (DTLTO)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:235
msgid ""
"Integrated Distributed ThinLTO (DTLTO) enables the distribution of backend "
"ThinLTO compilations via external distribution systems, such as "
"Incredibuild, during the traditional link step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:239
msgid ""
"The implementation is documented here: <https://llvm.org/docs/DTLTO.html>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:241
msgid "Command-Line Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:243
msgid "DTLTO requires the LLD linker (`-fuse-ld=lld`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:245
msgid "`-fthinlto-distributor=<path>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:246
msgid "Specifies the `<path>` to the distributor process executable for DTLTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:247
msgid "If specified, ThinLTO backend compilations will be distributed by LLD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:249
msgid "`-Xthinlto-distributor=<arg>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:250
msgid ""
"Passes `<arg>` to the distributor process (see `-fthinlto-distributor=`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:251
msgid "Can be specified multiple times to pass multiple options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:252
msgid "Multiple options can also be specified by separating them with commas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:254
msgid ""
"If `-fthinlto-distributor=` is specified, Clang supplies the path to a "
"compiler to be executed remotely to perform the ThinLTO backend "
"compilations. Currently, this is Clang itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:260
msgid ""
"Compilation is unchanged from ThinLTO. DTLTO options need to supplied for "
"the link step:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:267
msgid "When using lld-link:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ThinLTO.md:273
msgid ""
"Note that currently, DTLTO is only supported in some LLD flavors. Support "
"can be added to other LLD flavours in the future. See [DTLTO](https://lld."
"llvm.org/DTLTO.html) for more information."
msgstr ""

